{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`rebar link <bug> <target> caused_by` refuses a target with no referencing commit through `caused_by_refusal` (`src/rebar/_commands/link_revert.py:91`, called from `link_core` at line 201 and the dry-run at line 240). A bug close with `--caused-by=<target>` writes the same `caused_by` edge through `_apply_caused_by` (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:335`), which calls `_write_link_event` directly (line 365) with provenance `explicit` and never consults `caused_by_refusal`. So the close records explicit edges that `link` refuses, and the escaped-defect lenses read them as proven attributions.\n\nReproduced 2026-11-03 in a sandbox store (temp git repo, `rebar.init_repo`, 1 unrelated commit, no remote): `rebar.link(bug, target, \"caused_by\")` raises exit 1 \"has no commit referencing it\"; `rebar.transition(bug, \"in_progress\", \"closed\", close_class=\"regression\", caused_by=target)` succeeds and the bug carries `caused_by -> target` with provenance `explicit`. Live evidence: frank-rocky-rat.\n\nRoot cause: story 77e7-1eec-7b52-46ed scoped the referencing-commit rule to the `link` surfaces. The close path writes the edge through the low-level writer, so the rule never runs there.\n\n## Policy decisions (with the evidence they rest on)\n\n1. **Refuse the close before any write.** Bug surprising-fruticose-herring (Gerrit 3259) set the precedent for an invalid explicit `--caused-by`: `resolve_explicit_caused_by` (`transition_close.py:280`), called from `transition_compute` (`src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:263`) before the start-work gate, the parent cascade, and `close_ticket`, raises `CommandError` (exit 1) and nothing is written. Its plan states the reason: the value is an operator statement, and a bad one is a mistake to surface, not to drop silently. Closing without the edge and warning would also lose the stated attribution with only a stderr line. A commit-less target gets the same treatment.\n2. **Blame-derived edges are not re-checked.** With a blank flag, `_resolve_caused_by_culprit` calls `rebar.metrics.blame.derive_caused_by` (`transition_close.py:332`), whose culprit is the ticket named by the blamed commit's own message (`_commit_ticket`, `src/rebar/metrics/blame.py:172`, used at line 213). A derived target therefore has a referencing commit by construction, and re-scanning would add a possible remote fetch to every close for no new evidence. The check applies to the explicit flag only.\n3. **The close's `--force` does not bypass this check.** `transition_compute` documents `force_reason` as bypassing \"the applicable start or close gate\"; the referencing-commit rule is a link-evidence rule, not a gate, and herring's refusal also ignores `force_reason`. The refusal message points the operator at a target whose commit carries the trailer, or at closing without `--caused-by` and recording the attribution with `rebar link`, which keeps that rule's single override on the `link` surface.\n4. **Check only when the close would write an edge.** `_apply_caused_by` writes nothing for a non-bug (line 349), for a self-target, or for a target already active on the bug (line 354). The check runs only when the close would write, so a close never fails over an edge it would not record.\n5. **Unverifiable is allowed**, exactly as on `link`: `caused_by_refusal` returns `None` when history is unreadable or a replica cannot be refreshed (`_absence_is_proven`, `link_revert.py:134`).\n\n## Approach\n\n- Add `refuse_unproven_caused_by(ticket_id, caused_by, tracker, code_root)` in `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py` (652 lines; `transition_close.py` is 776 of the 800 cap). It returns immediately for a blank `caused_by`; otherwise reduces the ticket and returns when it is not a bug, the target equals the ticket, or the target is already in `_active_caused_by_targets(state)` (`transition_close.py:260`). Otherwise it calls the existing `caused_by_refusal(\"caused_by\", caused_by, tracker, code_root)` unchanged and, on a reason, raises `CommandError(returncode=1)` with \"Nothing was written; the ticket keeps its status and its caused_by links.\" No link/unlink code is edited (lionly-squarish-xantus is changing that area concurrently).\n- Call it in `transition_compute` directly after `resolve_explicit_caused_by` (line 263), passing `repo_root_str`, which is `config.repo_root(repo_root)`, the same code root `link_core` scans via `_code_root`. `resolve_explicit_caused_by` returns `\"\"` for non-close targets, so non-close transitions skip the check. The call adds no branch to `transition_compute`, so its complexity ceiling is unchanged.\n- CLI, library, and MCP closes all reach `transition_compute`, so 1 call covers every surface.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py`: new helper and 1 call.\n- `tests/unit/test_caused_by_commitless_panther.py` (new): regression tests.\n\n## Testing\n\nTests are written first and must fail on current main where marked. Sandbox fixture: temp git repo, `rebar.init_repo`, 1 unrelated commit, no remote (so absence is proven).\n\n- Commit-less explicit target on a bug close: `rebar.transition(..., caused_by=target)` raises `RebarError` with returncode 1 and \"no commit referencing\"; the bug stays `in_progress` and has no `caused_by` edge. (Fails before the fix.)\n- Target with a referencing commit (`rebar-ticket:` trailer): close succeeds and records the edge with provenance `explicit`.\n- Repo with no commits (unverifiable): close succeeds and records the edge, as `link` allows it.\n- Target already active on the bug: close succeeds; the edge keeps its `link_uuid`.\n- Non-bug (task) close with a commit-less `caused_by`: close succeeds.\n- Blank flag with `derive_caused_by` monkeypatched to return a commit-less target: close succeeds and the edge is `derived`, pinning decision 2.\n- Regression: `tests/unit/test_caused_by_unresolved_herring.py`, `tests/unit/test_caused_by_dedup_10d0.py`, `tests/unit/test_caused_by_provenance.py`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_caused_by_autoderive.py`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_caused_by_relation.py`, `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A bug close whose explicit `--caused-by` target has no referencing commit is refused before any write (exit 1, status and `caused_by` edges unchanged), matching `link`'s refusal; blame-derived edges, unverifiable history, already-active targets, and non-bug closes are not refused. Verified by `tests/unit/test_caused_by_commitless_panther.py`, which drives a commit-less target through `rebar.transition(..., caused_by=...)` and fails on the pre-fix tree.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `pytest` on the 6 regression files listed under Testing passes, and `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0 with the worktree `.venv/bin` first on PATH; results recorded in a ticket comment.\n  provenance: environment=local fix-panther worktree at the change's commit; principal=the operator's local user; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — same make targets and pytest that CI's Verified job runs\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The Gerrit change reaches `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` and merges to main.\n  provenance: environment=rebar Gerrit; principal=the configured Gerrit bot identity; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Gerrit REST change detail"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793702373802255001,"uuid":"9dbd4fbe-7fad-4731-9270-55e2dde1a784"}